        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks are a profound precision-measurement invention with exceptional consequences for timekeeping, metrology, and fundamental tests.",
        "attribution": "Katori originated the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept, while Ye made defining experimental advances toward leading clock performance.",
        "maturity": "Independent laboratories have established outstanding accuracy and reproducibility, with clear scientific and technological use.",
